<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ballari</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bellary</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ballari, formerly Bellary, is a city in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, known for the fort on the great granite rock that overlooks it. The surrounding region, rich in iron ore, has a long history: the earliest Pallava charters of the fourth century record grants of land there, and it later lay at the heart of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a>, whose capital Hampi is nearby.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ballari.jpg" alt="Ballari" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ravibhalli · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BELLARY_FORT_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
